{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105930-minor-template-ish-doubly-soul-d","id":1105930,"title":"[Minor Template-ish] Doubly Soul'd","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-20T20:54:27-07:00","id":1105930,"title":"[Minor Template-ish] Doubly Soul'd","content":"<span style=\"color:#008000\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Spiritual Excess [Persistent]</span></span><br /> You have an extra soul that got tethered to your body <i>somehow</i> - you feel more self-assured, and people can instinctively pick you out of a crowd. As a result, you have an additional dot of Integrity - this can allow you to reach an Integrity of 11, which grants you a +3 bonus on Breaking Point rolls and a +4 bonus to Abjuration rolls. If you would gain the Soulless condition, you may resolve this condition instead. Similarly, you may resolve this condition at any time to end the Soulless condition without resolving it.<br /> <b>Gaining the Condition:</b> Have another soul stuffed into your body while you aren't Soulless.<br /> <b>Resolving the Condition:</b> Have your soul removed; slot your second soul into the hole left by the first.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Take a Beat whenever your conspicuousness gets you into trouble.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Soul Taker [\u2022\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mortal, the Integrity advantage.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You may steal or give a soul to other willing mortals through your breath. By placing your mouth over theirs and spending a dot of Willpower, you may choose to either inhale their soul or exhale your own. If you inhale their soul, they gain the Soulless condition and you gain the Spiritual Excess condition - if you exhale your own, it's vice-versa.<br /> <b>Special: </b>You can only safely hold one extra soul this way - attempting to give someone the Spiritual Excess condition twice just makes the soul dribble away into the aether.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Devour the Soul [\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Taker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You may consume a soul you have taken with a moment's thought. When you do, you immediately gain 1xp and resolve the Spiritual<br /> Excess condition. More importantly, it satisfies hunger as if you've eaten a three-course meal, feels wonderful, and destroys the soul in question.<br /> <b>Special:</b> If you also have Name the Soul and happen to devour your <i>own</i> soul, you may choose to immediately trade in Name the Soul for two additional dots of Willpower instead of suffering the drawbacks of that merit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Embody the Soul [\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Taker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> As long as you have the Spiritual Excess condition, you may spend Willpower to do up to three of the following:<br /> \u2022 Downgrade a level of Aggravated damage to Lethal.<br /> \u2022 Downgrade a level of Lethal damage to Bashing.<br /> \u2022 Heal a level of Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Name the Soul [\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Taker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have imprinted your name and identity into your soul. You can always identify your own, original soul - you can identify its current host with a glance, and anyone who resolves the Soulless condition due to your soul also changes their Vice to match yours. As long as your soul is in your body, you take a Beat whenever you regain Willpower through your Virtue or Vice, and you cannot be Possessed or Claimed by ephemeral beings.<br /> <b>Drawbacks:</b> If your soul dissipates, it's an immediate Breaking Point at -5, and you immediately lose the Spiritual Excess condition (if you had it) - the soul in question is painfully coughed out. On the plus side, Sanctity of Merits does apply.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Store the Soul [\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Soul Taker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You may use Soul Taker on inanimate objects, as long as they could symbolically hold your breath. As long as an object holds a soul, you may retrieve it for a single point of Willpower (instead of a dot) - however, opening the container causes the soul to dissipate within a few seconds unless measures are taken to stop it (inhaling it again definitely counts).<br /> <b>Special:</b> If you also have Name the Soul, you do not age and cannot die due to Aggravated damage as long as your soul is stored in an inanimate object.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Unbind the Soul [\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Taker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You may use Soul Taker on yourself, granting yourself both of the Soulless and Spiritual Excess conditions with a deep breath. As long as you have the Soulless condition, you lose your shadow - as a result, you don't show up in mirrors, and cameras treat you as if you were invisible. Additionally, other characters may fulfill their Vice by ignoring your presence, regardless of what their Vice normally is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-21-2017, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T23:52:33-07:00","id":1105964,"title":"","content":"anuther great one i love this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:16:27-07:00","id":1106281,"title":"","content":"Can you spell out how the Special line for Devour the Soul works, and the second effect for Unbind the Soul? I think I get them, but clarification would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T19:43:46-07:00","id":1116647,"title":"","content":"Sorry for not answering sooner - I'm still getting used to working full weeks, and I've basically been stumbling around in a fugue for the last few weeks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105930-minor-template-ish-doubly-soul-d?p=1106281#post1106281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you spell out how the Special line for Devour the Soul works, and the second effect for Unbind the Soul? I think I get them, but clarification would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Devour The Soul, my intent (as far as I could remember) was that you'd get two dots of Willpower that don't count towards your cap. In retrospect, both of those are... a bit off. In retrospect, Devour the Soul can lose the special line.<br /> <br /> As for Unbind the Soul, the best way to put it is with an example:<br /> <br /> Stanley Soul-Drinker has Unbind the Soul, and uses it on themselves (because Patty Police is coming to arrest him for unspecified naughtiness). When she shows up, she can claim one Willpower from fulfilling her vice by ignoring him. It's not like she gains &quot;Ignore Stanley&quot; as a full vice - it only exists for the purposes of gaining Willpower (or whatever other things might happen due to fulfilling her Vice).<br /> <br /> Make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:03:49-07:00","id":1116788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105930-minor-template-ish-doubly-soul-d?p=1116647#post1116647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for not answering sooner - I'm still getting used to working full weeks, and I've basically been stumbling around in a fugue for the last few weeks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For Devour The Soul, my intent (as far as I could remember) was that you'd get two dots of Willpower that don't count towards your cap. In retrospect, both of those are... a bit off. In retrospect, Devour the Soul can lose the special line.<br /> <br /> As for Unbind the Soul, the best way to put it is with an example:<br /> <br /> Stanley Soul-Drinker has Unbind the Soul, and uses it on themselves (because Patty Police is coming to arrest him for unspecified naughtiness). When she shows up, she can claim one Willpower from fulfilling her vice by ignoring him. It's not like she gains &amp;quot;Ignore Stanley&amp;quot; as a full vice - it only exists for the purposes of gaining Willpower (or whatever other things might happen due to fulfilling her Vice).<br /> <br /> Make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But while that makes a certain kind of sense, why would she want to? Gaining the Willpower is opt-in and this scenario has her more incentivised toward catching him. Is it just carrot over stick (such as requiring Willpower spent to not ignore them)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T03:08:54-07:00","id":1121241,"title":"","content":"<s>Can you have more than one instance of the Spiritual Excess Condition (can you bind more than 1-2 souls to yourself)?</s><br /> <br /> Can you re-assert a new soul as &quot;yours&quot; if your old soul is destroyed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  1st question answered. 07-27-2017, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:10:28-07:00","id":1121251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105930-minor-template-ish-doubly-soul-d?p=1121241#post1121241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you have more than one instance of the Spiritual Excess Condition (can you bind more than 1-2 souls to yourself)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That one was answered in the merit itself<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"